#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7737
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Technicians use impulse components to fix or enhance impulse engines or "
"related impulse systems."
msgstr "Technicians use impulse components to fix or enhance impulse engines or related impulse systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7741
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers use warp components to fix or enhance warp engines, warp cores and/"
"or other related warp technology based systems."
msgstr "Engineers use warp components to fix or enhance warp engines, warp cores and/or other related warp technology based systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7745
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Technicians use shield components to enhance or fix shield capacitors, "
"shield charging systems and other shield or energy field generation systems."
msgstr "Technicians use shield components to enhance or fix shield capacitors, shield charging systems and other shield or energy field generation systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7749
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers and technicians use tractor components to repair or enhance "
"systems designed to pull objects towards the ship."
msgstr "Engineers and technicians use tractor components to repair or enhance systems designed to pull objects towards the ship."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7753
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Technicians use repulsor components to repair or enhance systems designed to "
"move objects away from the ship."
msgstr "Technicians use repulsor components to repair or enhance systems designed to move objects away from the ship."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7757
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers and weapon systems repair specialists use beam components to fix, "
"improve and/or tune beam weapons or related beam systems."
msgstr "Engineers and weapon systems repair specialists use beam components to fix, improve and/or tune beam weapons or related beam systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7761
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Repair crew use optic components in a variety of ship systems. Optic "
"components serve as the information pathways and linkages between many ship "
"systems"
msgstr "Repair crew use optic components in a variety of ship systems. Optic components serve as the information pathways and linkages between many ship systems"

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7765
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers often use robotic components to facilitate missile loading. Other "
"typical systems needing robotic components include medical bays, food "
"preparation, automated repair systems, etc."
msgstr "Engineers often use robotic components to facilitate missile loading. Other typical systems needing robotic components include medical bays, food preparation, automated repair systems, etc."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7769
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Some of the esoteric ship systems have specialized material requirements. "
"These are typically satisfied with a filament component of some kind"
msgstr "Some of the esoteric ship systems have specialised material requirements. These are typically satisfied with a filament component of some kind"

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7773
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers use transporter components to fix systems designed to move objects "
"from one location to another. The movement methods range from simple belt "
"rollers to atomic disassembly and reassembly."
msgstr "Engineers use transporter components to fix systems designed to move objects from one location to another. The movement methods range from simple belt rollers to atomic disassembly and reassembly."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7777
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Repair crew use sensor components to fix or repair those systems that "
"support the Science console in gathering information about the universe "
"around the ship."
msgstr "Repair crew use sensor components to fix or repair those systems that support the Science console in gathering information about the universe around the ship."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7781
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Technicians use communication components to fix the various systems used to "
"connect the ship to other ships, stations and/or alien entities on the Relay "
"console."
msgstr "Technicians use communication components to fix the various systems used to connect the ship to other ships, stations and/or alien entities on the Relay console."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7785
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Technicians use autodoc components to repair or maintain the automated "
"medical facilities used on many ships in place of a medical doctor or "
"medical staff."
msgstr "Technicians use autodoc components to repair or maintain the automated medical facilities used on many ships in place of a medical doctor or medical staff."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7789
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers need lifter components for a variety of systems needing to "
"temporarily move mechanisms or portions of mechanisms against the "
"acceleration or gravity aboard a ship."
msgstr "Engineers need lifter components for a variety of systems needing to temporarily move mechanisms or portions of mechanisms against the acceleration or gravity aboard a ship."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7793
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers use android components to build, repair and maintain androids that "
"serve on ships. Repair crews on many ships consist largely of androids."
msgstr "Engineers use android components to build, repair and maintain androids that serve on ships. Repair crews on many ships consist largely of androids."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7797
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Technicians and engineers use nanites in a number of systems including "
"shield, reactor, impulse engines, jump drives and warp drives. The nanites "
"are programmed to fix things at the molecular level, often in conditions "
"hazardous to organic beings such as humans."
msgstr "Technicians and engineers use nanites in a number of systems including shield, reactor, impulse engines, jump drives and warp drives. The nanites are programmed to fix things at the molecular level, often in conditions hazardous to organic beings such as humans."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7801
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"With all the automated systems on a ship, technicians often need software "
"components to upgrade or adjust systems."
msgstr "With all the automated systems on a ship, technicians often need software components to upgrade or adjust systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7805
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Many systems have specialized circuits that need upgrading or replacing via "
"one or more circuit components."
msgstr "Many systems have specialised circuits that need upgrading or replacing via one or more circuit components."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7809
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"Batteries on a ship range in size from the ones that provide most of the "
"energy to run the ship to tiny ones used in EVA space suits. Battery "
"components help maintain and improve these systems."
msgstr "Batteries on a ship range in size from the ones that provide most of the energy to run the ship to tiny ones used in EVA space suits. Battery components help maintain and improve these systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7815
msgctxt "explainGoodsComponent-comms"
msgid ""
"These are the typical component goods available. Which one would you like a "
"greater explanation of?"
msgstr "These are the typical component goods available. Which one would you like a greater explanation of?"

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7829
msgctxt "explainGoodsTrade-comms"
msgid ""
"These are the typical trade goods available. Which one would you like a "
"greater explanation of?"
msgstr "These are the typical trade goods available. Which one would you like a greater explanation of?"

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7835
msgctxt "explainGoodsTrade-comms"
msgid ""
"Many people want or need food to sustain themselves or to enjoy. A good "
"Relay officer will try to keep at least one food on board for the potential "
"trade benefit. When offered for sale, it's usually very cheap."
msgstr "Many people want or need food to sustain themselves or to enjoy. A good Relay officer will try to keep at least one food on board for the potential trade benefit. When offered for sale, it's usually very cheap."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7839
msgctxt "explainGoodsTrade-comms"
msgid ""
"Many people need medicine to cure illness or symptoms associated with "
"illness. Medicine is almost as cheap as food. The trade benefits are usually "
"very high. A good Relay officer will try to keep at least on medicine on "
"board for the potential trade benefit."
msgstr "Many people need medicine to cure illness or symptoms associated with illness. Medicine is almost as cheap as food. The trade benefits are usually very high. A good Relay officer will try to keep at least on medicine on board for the potential trade benefit."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7843
msgctxt "explainGoodsTrade-comms"
msgid ""
"A luxury good is anything someone considers valuable. Luxury types include "
"jewelry, specialized clothing, rare art, etc. The trade value of luxury is "
"not as high as food or medicine, but can still give some trade benefit. A "
"good Relay officer will be watching for relatively low priced luxury which "
"can be used to trade for higher priced components or minerals."
msgstr "A luxury good is anything someone considers valuable. Luxury types include jewelry, specialised clothing, rare art, etc. The trade value of luxury is not as high as food or medicine, but can still give some trade benefit. A good Relay officer will be watching for relatively low priced luxury which can be used to trade for higher priced components or minerals."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7857
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"These are the typical mineral goods available. Which one would you like a "
"greater explanation of?"
msgstr "These are the typical mineral goods available. Which one would you like a greater explanation of?"

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7863
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"Nickel is one of the most common metals found among asteroids. As such, it "
"has become the defacto standard metal for most of the structure of ships."
msgstr "Nickel is one of the most common metals found among asteroids. As such, it has become the defacto standard metal for most of the structure of ships."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7867
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"Platinum has electronic, explosive and medical applications, so techniciams "
"use it to repair and upgrade a variety of ship systems."
msgstr "Platinum has electronic, explosive and medical applications, so techniciams use it to repair and upgrade a variety of ship systems."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7871
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"Civilians and military technicians value gold for a variety of reasons "
"including use in jewelry and electronics."
msgstr "Civilians and military technicians value gold for a variety of reasons including use in jewelry and electronics."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7875
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"Due to its high potential for energy storage, engineers value dilithium in "
"ship engines and shields."
msgstr "Due to its high potential for energy storage, engineers value dilithium in ship engines and shields."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7879
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"Designers and engineers use tritanium in many aspects of ship construction "
"due to how it interacts with warp fields and jump mechanics."
msgstr "Designers and engineers use tritanium in many aspects of ship construction due to how it interacts with warp fields and jump mechanics."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7883
msgctxt "explainGoodsMineral-comms"
msgid ""
"Engineers value cobalt due to its magnetic, alloy and energy storage "
"applications."
msgstr "Engineers value cobalt due to its magnetic, alloy and energy storage applications."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7911
msgctxt "station-comms"
msgid "You need to stay docked for that action."
msgstr "You need to stay docked for that action."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7920
msgctxt "ammo-comms"
msgid "We do not deal in weapons of mass destruction."
msgstr "We do not deal in weapons of mass destruction."

#: scripts/scenario_38_allies_and_enemies.lua:7925
